{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And the Egyptians will hear.</b> Moses reasoned that when the blessed El said ״אַכֶּנּוּ בַדֶּבֶר״ (Numbers 14:12), the intent would be to strike them all immediately, and he was moved to ask what would become of His great Name, and said: behold, the Egyptians will hear at once that You killed these suddenly, and they will say that You acted out of inability to prevail over the inhabitants of this land. For they indeed saw that You brought this people up from among them by Your power, and they also heard that You, HaShem, are in the midst of this people — so they will not reckon that their downfall was because You abandoned them on account of their sin."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:46.845927805Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}